      "content": "#include \"knn.h\"\n\n#define BLOCK 128\n\nstatic void insert_distance(char *restrict labels, float *restrict distances, int k, float d, char label) {\n    for (int x = 0; x < k; x++) {\n        if (d < distances[x] || distances[x] == -1) {\n            for (int y = k - 1; y > x; y--) {\n                distances[y] = distances[y - 1];\n                labels[y] = labels[y - 1];\n            }\n\n            distances[x] = d;\n            labels[x] = label;\n\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    char * labels = (char *) malloc(sizeof(char) * k);\n    float * distances = (float *) malloc(sizeof(float) * k);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        labels[i] = -1;\n        distances[i] = -1;\n    }\n\n    const float px = to_evaluate.x, py = to_evaluate.y;\n\n    float block_d[BLOCK];\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        Group g = groups[i];\n        int len = g.length;\n\n        for (int base = 0; base < len; base += BLOCK) {\n            int count = len - base;\n            if (count > BLOCK) count = BLOCK;\n\n            // Compute distances into a contiguous local buffer.\n            for (int j = 0; j < count; j++) {\n                Point q = g.points[base + j];\n                float dx = q.x - px;\n                float dy = q.y - py;\n                block_d[j] = dx * dx + dy * dy;\n            }\n\n            // Update the k-smallest arrays in the original point order.\n            for (int j = 0; j < count; j++) {\n                insert_distance(labels, distances, k, block_d[j], g.label);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    qsort(labels, k, sizeof(char), compare_for_sort);\n\n    char most_frequent = labels[0];\n    int most_frequent_count = 1;\n    int current_frequency = 1;\n\n    for (int i = 1; i < k; i++) {\n        if (labels[i] != labels[i - 1]) {\n            if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n                most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\n                most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n            }\n\n            current_frequency = 1;\n        } else {\n            current_frequency++;\n        }\n\n        if (i == k - 1 && current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n            most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\n            most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n        }\n    }\n\n    return most_frequent;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\n    \n    Group * groups = (Group *) malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\n    }\n\n    int k = parse_k();\n\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\n\n    printf(\"%c\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\n}\n",
      "path": "src/knn.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Reducing the block size from 256 to 128 improves L1 cache residency for both the distance buffer and the point reads during each chunk, while hoisting the query coordinates out of all loops removes redundant loads. Adding restrict qualifiers to insert_distance helps the compiler disambiguate the label/distance arrays, potentially enabling better code generation in the insertion loop.",
  "notes": "Only src/knn.c is modified; knn.h and other files remain untouched. The change preserves exact iteration order and tie-breaking semantics because each block's distances are inserted in the same point order as before.",
